{
  "case_id": "2020-19-547",
  "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (United States Fish and Wildlife Service)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The December 2013 draft biological opinions are privileged, predecisional, deliberative material. They were written by staff at the Services as a recommendation to agency decisionmakers about the position the Services should adopt in the ongoing consultation with the EPA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. Counsel, the -- I'd like to follow up with the Chief Justice's line. The -- what if there were not a regulation that prohibited the issuance of a final opinion before or while the draft was under review by the requesting agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Guarnieri, could I focus on the part of your argument which is that the relevant decisionmakers were still working on the draft and give you a hypothetical, which is that there was -- the draft came to the relevant decisionmaker, and he looked at it and he realized that it was going to cause a big problem for the EPA, and so he said: You know, I'm not going to send this over. I'm going to give the EPA head a call and just tell him everything in it, and that will ensure that there's nothing FOIA-able that -- in this document. What -- what would your answer to that be? You know, he has the document, he's not working on it, but -- but he doesn't want to make it FOIA-able. And can he end- run this in that way?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Good morning, counsel. Let's say EPA had decided at the end of it to just withdraw its rule and -- and give up, at least for the time being, maybe come back to it in five or 10 years. Would that be a final decision? And, if so, would that have made the last draft that the Service gave to EPA discoverable or not in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would just emphasize again, as I've tried to several times this morning, that -- that there can be no real dispute on the facts of this case, that the decisionmakers at the Services did not make a final decision in December 2013."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Guarnieri",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The record is clear that they did not make a final decision in the ongoing consultation until May of 2014. And when they made that final decision, they --they released an 85-page joint opinion with -- with several hundred pages of appendices explaining to the public the reasoning that led them to issue a no jeopardy opinion in this particular consultation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sanjay Narayan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. NARAYAN: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I'd like to begin with the standard that follows from Sears and which should resolve this case. If a document explains the decision made by the agency with appreciable legal consequences, Exemption 5 does not apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: So how do you determine that? The -- the government says as"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So we're talking about that draft biological opinion, and it has two things about it: One, we're going to negotiate this with EPA; and, two, private people, who are nothing to do with the EPA, can get a hold under FOIA of that document. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I guess I'm asking you to abstract up a level with me, counsel, and say: You know, I think you'd agree here that EPA got to a better result thanks to the Services' informal interventions, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the agency decision? I would -- I would have thought that the way to do this is to start by figuring out what is the decision, capital D decision, and then everything that led up to that decision is --is predecisional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the second question I wanted to ask is the need for clear rules in the FOIA context. So the -- the need for that, I think, is multi-pronged."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it true that the draft biological opinion, that second one in the hierarchy, is always FOIA-able and that there's no controversy"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My next question has to do with the -- what you characterized as the legal effect of this document. Why was it a legal effect as opposed to simply a practical effect when having this document caused the EPA to abandon the 2013 regulation and then move on to the 2014 regulation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But how can a draft opinion give rise to that legal consequence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In our view, the general rule here should be a clear bright-line test that, until a biological opinion is signed and formally issued, there is no final decision in an interagency consultation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-547",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c15656ca357998e9232b0fc2c6fe94d84e70b8eaff2f28f962d302e2dfb6e44c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c15656ca3579-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
